const businessTrust = "Georgia does NOT have a specific statutory business trust act like Ohio or Pennsylvania. Business trusts / Massachusetts trusts in Georgia are treated under common law principles as supplemented by the Georgia Trust Code (O.C.G.A. Title 53, Ch. 12). Georgia recognizes business trusts under common law — the trust code's general provisions apply to express trusts including those used for business purposes. Georgia does not require filing a business trust instrument with the Secretary of State. There is no separate business trust entity statute. Business trusts are generally treated as common law trusts for most purposes.";
